{"name":"Forest Floor","hex":"#555142","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"},{"term":"floor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["floor function"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The interior bottom or surface of a house or building; the supporting surface of a room.","The bottom surface of a natural structure, entity, or space (e.g. cave, forest, ocean, desert, etc.); the ground (surface of the Earth)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Forest Floor","blocks":[{"text":"Forest Floor is the third studio album by Scottish jazz pianist Fergus McCreadie, released on 8 April 2022 by Edition Records. The album was recorded 6–8 July 2021 by McCreadie, bassist David Bowden, and drummer Stephen Henderson. It was shortlisted for the Mercury Prize and won the Scottish Album of the Year Award. The lead single \"Law Hill\" was released 28 March."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Forest_Floor.album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_Floor"},{"title":"Forest floor","blocks":[{"text":"The forest floor, also called detritus or duff, is the part of a forest ecosystem that mediates between the living, aboveground portion of the forest and the mineral/humus-rich soil, principally composed of decaying plant litter and other dead plant matters such as coarse woody debris. In some countries, like Canada, forest floor refers to L, F and H organic horizons. It hosts a wide variety of decomposers and predators, including invertebrates, fungi, algae, bacteria, and archaea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Forest-floor076.jpg/330px-Forest-floor076.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest_floor"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest"},{"title":"Floor","blocks":[{"text":"A floor is the bottom surface of typically an enclosed space such as a room or vehicle. Floors vary from simple dirt in a cave to many layered surfaces made with modern technology. Floors may be stone, wood, bamboo, metal, or any other material that can support the expected load."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Parquet_flooring_in_Mus%C3%A9e_des_arts_d%C3%A9coratifs_de_Strasbourg.jpg/330px-Parquet_flooring_in_Mus%C3%A9e_des_arts_d%C3%A9coratifs_de_Strasbourg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png/500px-Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png/1280px-Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png/500px-Rainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boreal Forest Floor in the Okanagan, British Columbia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainy_Early_Winter_Morning_on_Kirschner_Mountain.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg/500px-Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg/1280px-Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg/500px-Pryor%27s_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bluebells (Hyacinthoides non-scripta, Pryor's Wood, Stevenage)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APryor's_Wood_Bluebells_2017-04-26-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Sarcodes_sanguinea_08080.jpg/500px-Sarcodes_sanguinea_08080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Sarcodes_sanguinea_08080.jpg/1280px-Sarcodes_sanguinea_08080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org